---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BenchmarkExplorer from '../components/BenchmarkExplorer';
---
<Layout title="Validation — PRINCE" description="Inspect PRINCE's frozen 110-interface retrospective evaluation, component-level uncertainty, and official BepiPred comparison.">
  <section class="page-hero wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Prince</a><span>/</span><span>Validation</span></div><span class="eyebrow">The evidence, with its edges showing</span><h1>Show the work.<br /><em>Keep the context.</em></h1><p class="lede">A frozen, retrospective evaluation. Explore what was measured, how it was counted, and where the uncertainty remains.</p><div class="metric-strip"><div><strong>110</strong><span>Test interfaces</span></div><div><strong>34</strong><span>Identity components</span></div><div><strong>28,845</strong><span>Test residues</span></div></div></section>
  <div class="wrap"><section class="content-section"><span class="eyebrow">01 / Patch selection</span><h2>Different questions.<br /><em>Different measures.</em></h2><p>How often does a proposed patch land mostly in the observed epitope? How often does it cover at least half of that epitope? These are separate binary outcomes, counted once per interface.</p><BenchmarkExplorer client:load /><p class="research-note" style="margin-top:20px">Interactive values are read directly from the bundled <a class="prose-link" href="/prince/site-uncertainty.json">site-uncertainty artifact</a>. All 110 interfaces were evaluated, covering 105 structural contexts with zero errors.</p></section>
  <section class="content-section"><span class="eyebrow">02 / Residue-level ranking</span><div class="two-column"><div><h2>The comparison.<br /><em>Without a victory lap.</em></h2></div><div><p>Per-interface metrics are averaged within identity components, then across components. These are not pooled-residue metrics and do not measure binder success.</p><p>Official BepiPred-3.0 was run on the same corrected labels. This comparison does not establish PRINCE superiority.</p></div></div><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Residue evaluation comparison"><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>AUROC · 95% CI</th><th>AUPRC · 95% CI</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>PRINCE fitted</td><td>0.64790 <small>0.62180–0.67218</small></td><td>0.13610 <small>0.11682–0.15726</small></td></tr><tr><td>Exposure only</td><td>0.64500 <small>0.61930–0.66820</small></td><td>0.13294 <small>0.11286–0.15353</small></td></tr><tr><td>Official BepiPred-3.0</td><td>0.65244 <small>0.60212–0.70186</small></td><td>0.19636 <small>0.14925–0.24551</small></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="research-note">BepiPred minus PRINCE: AUROC +0.00454 (95% CI −0.04914 to +0.05747); AUPRC +0.06026 (+0.01842 to +0.10415). BepiPred’s upstream training overlap is unknown. <a class="prose-link" href="/prince/bepipred-comparison.json">Inspect the comparison.</a></p></section>
  <section class="content-section two-column"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / Know the denominator</span><h2>The data<br /><em>behind the split.</em></h2><p>The original SAbDab-derived manifest contained 8,241 interfaces. After connected identity grouping and a 20-per-component cap, 6,937 were retained.</p><p>Of 649 cached feature interfaces, 60 were excluded by the repaired cap. The remaining <strong>589</strong> were actually used: 340 training, 139 validation, and 110 test interfaces.</p><a class="text-link" href="/prince/connected-manifest.csv" download>Download the manifest <span>↓</span></a></div><div><h3>What stays outside the claim</h3><ul class="prose-list"><li>Zero accession or exact-sequence overlap across splits does not imply homology disjointness.</li><li>These are bound-complex conformations, with antibodies removed before structural scoring.</li><li>Features had been explored previously. This is a retrospective reanalysis, not an untouched external holdout.</li><li>Antibody epitope labels are not wet-lab minibinder outcomes.</li></ul></div></section>
  <section class="content-section two-column"><div><span class="eyebrow">04 / Negative findings matter too</span><h2>No effect<br />is <em>still a result.</em></h2><p>The implemented filter removed 0 of 5,526 fitted patches and 0 of 5,581 exposure-only patches. Filtered and unfiltered results are identical: no filter benefit was measured.</p></div><div><h3>Evidence ranking remains unevaluated.</h3><p>Independent reviewed literature labels were not available for this evaluation, so a literature-evidence ablation was not run.</p><p>The hand-set designability profile is also unvalidated for minibinder designability. Its residue AUROC in the supplied evaluation is 0.5069.</p><div class="callout">These results do not establish a calibrated binder-success probability or a reliable improvement over exposure alone.</div></div></section>
  <div class="inline-cta"><h2>Read it. <em>Recheck it.</em></h2><a class="button" href="/resources/">Get the artifacts <span>↗</span></a></div></div>
</Layout>
